Chrome's passkeys page (chrome://settings/passkeys, which Settings › Passwords › Manage Passkeys…
opens) says under its title that the passkeys "aren't saved to your Google Account". ilo signs in to
no Google account, so its words say only where they are: on this Mac, or in Windows Hello on this
computer (#3619). The page's other words and its edit and delete dialogs name no account. A changed
message has no translation until one is written, so other languages show these English words.

--- a/chrome/app/settings_strings.grdp
+++ b/chrome/app/settings_strings.grdp
@@ -838,12 +838,12 @@
       </message>
     <if expr="is_win">
       <message name="IDS_AUTOFILL_MANAGE_PASSKEYS_SUB_TITLE_WIN" desc="A warning on a page where the user can see and delete passkeys saved on their computer. It communicates that the passkeys shown are stored in Windows Hello, which is a Microsoft product name, and not in the user's Google account. For consistency, the word 'passkey' is in the glossary with translations already suggested.">
-        These passkeys are saved to Windows Hello on this computer. They aren't saved to your Google Account.
+        These passkeys are saved to Windows Hello on this computer.
       </message>
     </if>
     <if expr="is_macosx">
       <message name="IDS_AUTOFILL_MANAGE_PASSKEYS_SUB_TITLE_MAC" desc="A warning on a page where the user can see and delete passkeys saved on their computer. For consistency, the word 'passkey' is in the glossary with translations already suggested.">
-        These passkeys are only saved on this device. They aren't saved to your Google Account.
+        These passkeys are saved on this Mac and nowhere else.
       </message>
     </if>
       <message name="IDS_AUTOFILL_MANAGE_PASSKEYS_SEARCH" desc="The label on a field that a user can use to search within a list of passkeys. For consistency, the word 'passkey' is in the glossary with translations already suggested.">
